OSD_Host: no <netdb.h>, no resolver and no gethostbyname() on wasm32-wasip1.

NO condition was available to extend at either site, which is the exception this directory's rules
allow and require to be stated. The only platform test in force here is the file-wide
`#ifndef _WIN32`, and excluding WASI from it sends WASI into the Windows branch below: the same
situation wasi-osd-chronometer.patch documents at its own include. Both guards are therefore new,
and both spell the same test.

The include is guarded AND the call site is guarded. <netdb.h> supplies both gethostbyname() and
struct hostent, and InternetAddress() declares one of those as a local, so guarding the include
alone would move the error rather than remove it.

Nothing else in this file changes: wasi-libc supplies uname() and gethostname(), both defined in
the Swift SDK sysroot's libc.a, so SystemVersion(), SystemId(), HostName() and MachineType() keep
working unmodified.

WHAT THE WASI BRANCH RETURNS: InternetAddress() returns an empty TCollection_AsciiString. It has
exactly one in-tree consumer, STEPConstruct_AP203Context::DefaultPersonAndOrganization
(STEPConstruct_AP203Context.cxx:160), which uses the address as a unique organisation id: it calls
SearchFromEnd(".") on the result, gets -1 for an empty string, skips the concatenation and leaves
the id as the literal "IP". A STEP file written from wasm therefore carries the organisation id
"IP" rather than "IP<a.b.c>", and nothing else in the file changes. Keeping the existing code under
an emulation is not an option on offer: there is no resolver on wasip1 to emulate.

Issue: https://github.com/SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift/issues/2173

diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Host.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Host.cxx
index ce00a9e8..947770c4 100644
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Host.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Host.cxx
@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@ const OSD_WhoAmI Iam = OSD_WHost;
   #include <cerrno>
 
   #include <sys/utsname.h> // For 'uname'
-  #include <netdb.h>       // This is for 'gethostbyname'
+  #ifndef __wasi__
+    #include <netdb.h> // This is for 'gethostbyname'
+  #endif
   #include <unistd.h>
   #include <cstdio>
 
@@ -156,6 +158,10 @@ int OSD_Host::AvailableMemory()
 
 TCollection_AsciiString OSD_Host::InternetAddress()
 {
+  #ifdef __wasi__
+  // wasi-libc has no <netdb.h>, no resolver and no host name lookup
+  return TCollection_AsciiString();
+  #else
   struct hostent          internet_address;
   int                     a, b, c, d;
   char                    buffer[16];
@@ -177,6 +183,7 @@ TCollection_AsciiString OSD_Host::InternetAddress()
   Sprintf(buffer, "%d.%d.%d.%d", a, b, c, d);
   result = buffer;
   return (result);
+  #endif
 }
 
